Z||000020||DaRkLoRD||07-29-2000||08:04 PM||||I agree, that post wasn't too nice. and I also agree that posts that are miss-spelled and all in caps, with no punctuation, are slightly hard to understand... (ok, very hard, at times.. hehe)<P>some people don't bother to put much effort into grammar or punctuation, and when some of them get any criticism of that, they take it personally. I think that's what happened here.. I've always been fairly good at spelling and grammar, so I too find it a bit annoying when others write stuff that isn't clear due to improper grammar or punctuation. I usually keep my mouth shut though.. yesterday at when I was getting some gas, a big truck pulled in behind me just as I was paying.. there was another truck pulling a big boat blocking the exit I was facing, so I just sat there and waited for the truck behind me to finish getting gas and then move so I could back out. one of the gas station attendants (the owner actually) came over and asked me to move my car up a bit, so the truck behind me would have more room.. it sounded like he said "move the h*ll up" but since he had a strong indian accent, I'm not sure.. (I'm no good with accents..) he had no reason to not ask me politely, so I assume he did and I just heard him wrong.. even though at that moment I was thinking "why the h*ll can't everyone just speak english??"<P>point is.. I get irritated by stuff like this as well, I just don't usually say anything. in situations like this, I usually try to see both sides of the issue.. anyway, I'm gonna shut up now before I make people mad at me or something.... <P>nothing personal against you either, I just don't like to see friends arguing.. I'll try to stay out of discussions like this in the future.............<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
